WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
K-12 walkthrough. A K-12 learning platform the district owns outright. Recorded on the zero-login demo: Northfield Public Schools, a fictional district running entirely in the browser.

2
00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:09.908
Northfield Public Schools · a fictional district: The zero-login demo runs the real EducateOS district application in your browser. Nothing you do is sent anywhere.

3
00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:18.241
Northfield Public Schools · a fictional district: A student and a teacher in every grade band, a parent, and the district office.

4
00:00:18.241 --> 00:00:23.019
Northfield Public Schools · a fictional district: The K-12 tour walks through it in nine screens, from first grade to the district office.

5
00:00:23.019 --> 00:00:27.972
Grade 1 · Mateo: Mateo retells a story: one step a screen, big type, and Read to me on every instruction.

6
00:00:27.972 --> 00:00:34.046
Grade 1 · Mateo: His Reading Buddy is a labelled simulation in the demo. Under each message: what Hall Monitor would decide.

7
00:00:34.046 --> 00:00:40.095
Grade 1 · Mateo: Off-topic requests are stopped before they reach the AI, and the tutor steers back to the story.

8
00:00:40.095 --> 00:01:03.148
Grade 1 · Mateo: He answers by voice: record, save, and play it back. No typing or reading needed.

9
00:01:03.148 --> 00:01:16.410
Grade 1 · Mateo: And draws how the story ended.

10
00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:24.699
Grade 1 · Mateo: He hands it in. His teacher sees it now, and his family once the teacher shares feedback.

11
00:01:24.699 --> 00:01:34.653
Grade 1 · Mr. Yazzie, teacher: Mr. Yazzie reviews Priya's retelling. Recordings and drawings arrive as submitted work.

12
00:01:34.653 --> 00:01:44.942
Grade 1 · Mr. Yazzie, teacher: A rubric written for six-year-olds. His scores become the official grade only when he approves it.

13
00:01:44.942 --> 00:01:50.868
Grade 1 · Mr. Yazzie, teacher: Sharing the feedback releases it to Priya and her family at the same moment.

14
00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:54.482
Teacher Studio · open courses: His semester came from Grade 1 Reading Foundations, a signed open course package from educateos.io.

15
00:01:54.482 --> 00:01:58.672
Teacher Studio · open courses: Each unit brings pages, activities, and a teacher guide and answer key that only teachers see.

16
00:01:58.672 --> 00:02:11.675
Teacher Studio · open courses: Add a course previews any of the 12 open courses as draft modules. Nothing he already has changes.

17
00:02:11.675 --> 00:02:17.959
Grade 4 · Abena: Grade 4: Abena's Homework Helper gives hints and sentence starters, never answers.

18
00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:28.185
Grade 4 · Abena: Asking it to do the graded work is redirected, and every message shows what Hall Monitor decided.

19
00:02:28.185 --> 00:02:36.558
Grade 7 · Chidi: Grade 7: Chidi's primary-source analysis of Hammurabi's laws, with his teacher's comment and rubric scores.

20
00:02:36.558 --> 00:02:45.506
World History 7 · Mr. Ortega, teacher: The gradebook holds official grades only: a score counts once the teacher records or approves it.

21
00:02:45.506 --> 00:02:54.263
Grade 9 · Amara: Grade 9: feedback and the official grade on an argument essay. Her Research & Essay Coach won't write it for her.

22
00:02:54.263 --> 00:02:59.591
Family · Rosa Delgado: Rosa Delgado follows Mateo in grade 1 and Lucía in grade 10, in two schools, with one sign-in.

23
00:02:59.591 --> 00:03:07.040
Family · Rosa Delgado: She sees what teachers have shared, never a child's drafts or private space.

24
00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.773
District office · Avery Admin: The district office: every class from kindergarten to grade 12, in one console.

25
00:03:12.773 --> 00:03:18.714
District office · Avery Admin: The course library: each course is checked against its publisher's signature before it is stored.

26
00:03:18.714 --> 00:03:23.307
District office · Avery Admin: Standards ship only where their licences allow. NGSS isn't built in, and the console says so.

27
00:03:23.307 --> 00:03:28.807
District-owned. Open source. Runs in your own Cloudflare account. Try the demo at educateos.io/demo, no sign-in. Apache-2.0. In development: no real students use EducateOS yet.
